@startuml object-note-signature-layout
'' PlantUML over Mermaid because this is a DATA LAYOUT: typed arrays with exact lengths, and the index relations
'' between them (a permutation, a group's range, a match's slide run, a bucket's chain of cells). A PlantUML object
'' diagram shows each array as a record with its type and length, packages group the arrays by the function that owns
'' them, links carry the indexing, and the formulas render as LaTeX; Mermaid has no object notation with per-record
'' fields inside coloured packages. The SVG renders byte-reproducibly (README §4).
'' Colours, from the shared palette: teal = what the renderer's platform hands the model (pdf.js's text runs, through
'' vinary.slides.evidence/page-runs, and the generator crypto.getRandomValues); orange = the pure model
'' vinary.slides.notes, one call of note-page-signature?: the palest orange packages group the arrays by the function
'' that owns them, and every array (the mid orange) is sized before it is filled.
!include _vv-theme.iuml

title The arrays of one comparison under F″ (scientific/14 §4.4): each sized before it is filled

object "slide runs" as SR RENDERER_TINT {
  <latex>r_s</latex> maps {:str s, :t [a b c d e f]}
  in page order (page-runs)
}
object "note runs" as NR RENDERER_TINT {
  <latex>r_j</latex> maps {:str s, :t [a b c d e f]}
  in page order (page-runs)
}
object "crypto.getRandomValues" as RNG RENDERER_TINT {
  the platform's cryptographic generator:
  one call per comparison with a match
}

package "by-height: the note page sorted by string, then height (no hash)" IR_FILL {
  object "runs" as U IR_TINT {
    <latex>p \le r_j</latex>: the upright runs
    whose :str is a string
  }
  object "strs · h" as SH IR_TINT {
    strs = js/Array p (the strings)
    h = Float64Array p (the heights)
  }
  object "order" as O IR_TINT {
    Int32Array p: the stable merge
    sort's permutation (sorted-runs;
    two buffers, swapped each pass)
  }
  object "strings · starts" as G IR_TINT {
    strings = js/Array p, the first G used
    starts = Int32Array G + 1
    group g = [starts[g], starts[g + 1])
  }
  object "hs · xs · ys" as HXY IR_TINT {
    Float64Array p each: the heights
    and origins, in sorted order
  }
}

package "note-page-signature?: count the matches, then build them" IR_FILL {
  object "s-runs · glyph-of" as S IR_TINT {
    s-runs = the n upright slide
    runs with a glyph
    glyph-of = Int32Array n
  }
  object "kept" as K IR_TINT {
    Int32Array 2n: slide run i keeps
    the sorted runs [kept[2i], kept[2i + 1])
  }
  object "mi · qls · qtx · qty" as MQ IR_TINT {
    mi = Int32Array M (the slide run)
    qls, qtx, qty = Float64Array M
    (the three cell quotients)
  }
}

package "copy-covers?: the call's own hash table" IR_FILL {
  object "tables" as T IR_TINT {
    Int32Array 6 144: one table of 256
    words per (axis, byte), 3 × 8 of them
  }
  object "axes" as AX IR_TINT {
    Int32Array 6M: per match, index-hash
    of each axis under each shift
  }
  object "heads · stamps" as HB IR_TINT {
    Int32Array B each
    <latex>B = \max(16,\ 2^{\lceil \log_2 2M \rceil})</latex>
    stamps[β] = the grid (1–8) that wrote heads[β]
  }
  object "nexts · last · ca · cb · cc · sums" as CELLS IR_TINT {
    nexts, last = Int32Array M
    ca, cb, cc, sums = Float64Array M
    one entry per cell, in the order first seen
  }
}

NR -[IR_BORDER]-> U : upright?, :str a string
U -[IR_BORDER]-> SH
SH -[IR_BORDER]-> O : <latex>< p \lceil \log_2 p \rceil</latex> comparisons\n(string, then height)
O -[IR_BORDER]-> G : one pass in sorted order:\na new group where the string changes
O -[IR_BORDER]-> HXY
SR -[IR_BORDER]-> S : upright?, glyphs > 0
S -[IR_BORDER]-> K : group-of: a binary search of strings;\nprefix-count twice within the group
G -[IR_BORDER]-> K
HXY -[IR_BORDER]-> K
K -[IR_BORDER]-> MQ : the count <latex>M \le C_m</latex>, else nil;\nthen one match per k in kept_i
HXY -[IR_BORDER]-> MQ : <latex>\sigma = hs_k / h_i</latex>
S -[IR_BORDER]-> MQ : slide run i: its height and origin
RNG -[RENDERER_BORDER]-> T : 6 144 fresh words each time
T -[IR_BORDER]-> AX
MQ -[IR_BORDER]-> AX : <latex>\lfloor q - s \rfloor</latex>, canonical bits
AX -[IR_BORDER]-> HB : <latex>\beta = (a_\ell \oplus a_x \oplus a_y) \wedge (B - 1)</latex>
HB -[IR_BORDER]-> CELLS : the chain: heads[β], then nexts
S -[IR_BORDER]-> CELLS : glyph-of[i] into sums,\nonce per cell (last)

legend right
  |= Colour |= Concept |
  |<#2D9574>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| what the renderer's platform hands the model: pdf.js's runs, the random words |
  |<#E67E22>&#160;&#160;&#160;&#160;| the pure model vinary.slides.notes: one call's arrays, grouped by the function that owns them |
  Lengths: <latex>p \le r_j \le C_r</latex>, <latex>n \le r_s \le C_r</latex>, <latex>G \le p</latex>, <latex>M \le C_m</latex>. In all <latex>O(r_s + r_j + M)</latex> words (§5.2).
endlegend
@enduml
